1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,582
Your phone may see invisible light.

2
00:00:02,582 --> 00:00:04,420
Try this simple experiment!

3
00:00:05,075 --> 00:00:06,774
Point a TV remote at your

4
00:00:06,774 --> 00:00:08,745
phone camera. Press a button.

5
00:00:08,745 --> 00:00:10,240
You may see a flicker.

6
00:00:10,908 --> 00:00:13,227
Many remotes use near-infrared light.

7
00:00:13,227 --> 00:00:14,982
Your eyes cannot see it, but

8
00:00:14,982 --> 00:00:16,862
a camera sensor may detect it.

9
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:19,804
Nothing? Try the front camera.

10
00:00:19,804 --> 00:00:21,470
Infrared filters vary.

11
00:00:21,470 --> 00:00:23,816
Not every remote uses infrared.

12
00:00:24,492 --> 00:00:26,278
This is not thermal imaging or

13
00:00:26,278 --> 00:00:27,529
seeing through walls.

14
00:00:27,529 --> 00:00:29,136
It is simply another way to

15
00:00:29,136 --> 00:00:30,446
detect a light signal.

16
00:00:31,117 --> 00:00:32,252
Try your remote.

17
00:00:32,252 --> 00:00:33,812
Did you see a flicker?

18
00:00:33,812 --> 00:00:35,798
Tell us which camera worked!
